# INTENTIONALLY EMPTY - no Source is registered by this module.
#
# SqsSource used to be listed here, "pre-registered for future
# auto-config". It was removed in sprint-23 (Story 1.2) for the same two
# reasons as its GCP twin (see the gcp-pubsub module's Source file):
#
#  1. NOT CONSTRUCTIBLE. Its constructors take (SqsClient, queueUrl) and
#     (SqsClient, queueUrl, maxNumberOfMessages, waitTimeSeconds) -
#     SqsSource.java:86 and SqsSource.java:107 - so ServiceLoader raised
#     ServiceConfigurationError on every discovery pass. AutoConfig
#     swallowed that error before Story 1.1.
#
#  2. Source IS NOT A ONE-PER-CLASSPATH CONTRACT. AutoConfig exposes no
#     singular source() accessor, only the plural sources()
#     (AutoConfig.java:264-266). A queue URL is per-stage wiring, not
#     per-environment configuration, so there is no honest no-arg
#     constructor to write.
#
# Story 1.2 AC 5 scoped the AWS entries as "fix only if it is a genuine
# no-arg constructor; otherwise leave the registration removed and flag
# it". It is not, so this is the removal branch, taken deliberately rather
# than by invention of a CULVERT_SQS_QUEUE_URL variable that no deployment
# sets.
#
# The class is unchanged and fully supported. Construct it per stage:
#     new SqsSource(client, queueUrl)
